From d1c4c53bce8ff171bb343e6967ec08e321eee96c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:10:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(layout)!: place an underfull scrolling strip at
 start, center or end

`layout.scrolling.center_underfull_strip` could only center a strip narrower than the viewport or start-align it. `underfull_strip` replaces it with three placements, so a workspace holding one or two windows can rest against either edge. The old names map onto the new ones: true is "center" (the default) and false is "start".

An end-aligned strip keeps its trailing edge pinned; while the strip fits, its windows resize from their leading edges, because dragging the trailing edge would push the strip past the edge it is anchored to. The names are axis-neutral: on a vertical strip start is the top edge and end the bottom one.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
