From 7eec2b3b8a6e7987244e47348ca604b8b5b09c19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:53:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(layout): keep interior strip boundaries draggable and
 re-judge rests on reload

An end-aligned strip that fits used to refuse the trailing edge of every
window, which made interior column boundaries undraggable even though they
take width from the next lane. Only the last column needs that refusal;
interior trailing boundaries now mirror the existing leading-boundary pair
span so both lanes keep their widths.

Reloading `layout.scrolling.underfull_strip` also left a live centered rest
with a stale scroll, drawing the strip up to half a viewport off. The layout
config apply path now treats that change as a reason to reconcile.

Also pins "center" parsing and the invalid-value diagnostic.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
