From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:15:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(layout): share the pair resize math and keep centre's
 growth symmetric
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The interior trailing branch was a hand-mirrored copy of the leading-edge
branch, and the mirror was inverted: a dragged column stopping at its client
maximum paid the remaining travel out of the next lane with no floor, so that
lane could shrink below the 0.15 minimum (306 -> 115 px on the review's probe).
Both edges now call one resizePair helper, which pins the dragged lane and lets
the far lane absorb the remaining travel exactly like the leading edge does.

The same branch also caught the default centre alignment, which silently
turned its interior drags from "the strip grows" into "the neighbour gives
way" — a behaviour change the docs promise does not happen. The branch is now
gated on end alignment.

Also: pin the replaced boolean key's unknown-key warning, reword the docs'
end-alignment paragraph, and trim the harness check to the live-only legs.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
